tara:TARA_1160697 a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:label "Lower He-Sea Point of the Triple Energizer" ;
    dc:description "The Lower He-Sea Point of the Triple Energizer meridian. One of the five Shu Points, the He-Sea point signifies the confluence of rivers in the sea, where the meridian qi is the most flourishing. In addition, each of the six fu organs has another He-Sea point in the three yang meridians of the foot, known as the Lower He-Sea point. The Lower He-Sea points are mostly employed to treat the disorders of the six fu organs in clinic." ;
    dcterms:bibliographicCitation "Chinese Acupuncture and Moxibustion. Edited by C. Xinnong, Rev. Ed., Foreign Languages Press, Beijing, China, 1999. Ch. 6, An Introduction to Acupunture Points, Sec. III, Specific Points. ISBN 978-7-119-01758-7." ;
